From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LNPANDY <lnp-andy@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:14:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] packing/nsp: derive shader map when only main duplicate
 labels shift

Commit 8d62601f switched main's duplicate shader selection in shader_split.py
from last-copy to checked first-copy, keeping every shader key, stage, package
and binary payload identical while shifting representative source labels and
package indices for executables with duplicate embedded shaders. Profiles that
have not yet been re-split under #2924 (over 20 games including Stardew Valley,
Animal Crossing: New Horizons and Captain Toad) stop at the strict whole-row
shader_map.tsv check when packing.

Add main_duplicate_label_change alongside dlc_only_shader_change and
compute_reader_additions in scripts/build_ipa_from_nsp.py. When every shader
key, stage, package, non-main source, fact table and pair table match, every
changed source stays within the same main-collected reader family, unrelated
packages keep their indices, and each package's new indices follow (source,
key) order, promote the build to a shader-only derived profile that preserves
registered cuts and analysis tables (c1_full.tsv, cb_extent.tsv) and caches a
verified pkg.dup.key proof. Also allow compatible main duplicate label shifts
on non-DLC rows inside dlc_only_shader_change so DLC + unrefreshed profiles do
not deadlock.

Verified against real Stardew Valley (0100E65002BB8000) and Captain Toad
(01009BF0072D4000) splits, plus 115 unit tests across test_nsp_incremental.py,
test_nsp_chain.py and test_split_representatives.py.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#3095
Reason: Derive shader map when only main duplicate labels shift after 8d62601f
Issue: none

